{"id":6768,"path":"/grammar-points/a1/verbs-infinitive-verbs-ing/","parentId":540,"order":155,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a1","depth":3,"title":"Verbs + to + infinitive and verbs + -ing","seo":{"title":"Verbs + to + infinitive and verbs + -ing - Test-English","description":"Learn how to use verbs with the infinitive and verbs ending in -ing in this A1 grammar lesson. Clear rules, chart and exercises. Practise now!","image":"/media/uploads/A1Grammar_Verbs-infinitive_Verbs-ing.png"},"modified":"2026-02-18T18:11:09","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct infinitive or -ing forms.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"550\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct infinitive or -ing forms to complete these sentences.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"551\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Complete the sentences using the <em>to</em> + infinitive or the -ing forms of the verbs in the list.</h5> <p></p> <p class=\"textBox\">close – cook – do – get up – play(x2) – see – <del>travel</del> – watch – water – work</p> <p><em>EXAMPLE: I’m planning ⇒ <span class=\"textGap\">to travel</span> to Egypt next year.</em><br> </p><div data-quiz=\"552\"></div> <p></p>"],"explanation":"<h2>Verbs + <strong>-ing</strong></h2> <p>Some verbs in English are followed by another verb in the <strong>-ing</strong> form. The most common of these verbs are <a href=\"/vocabulary/a2/hobbies-and-free-time-a2-english-vocabulary/\">verbs of liking</a> and disliking: <strong>love, like, enjoy, don’t mind, don’t like, hate</strong>. If we use another verb after these verbs, it often takes the&nbsp;<strong>-ing&nbsp;</strong>form.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I <span><strong>love going</strong></span> to the gym.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>like reading</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>enjoy travelling</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>don’t mind cooking</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>don’t like doing</strong></span> homework.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>hate getting</strong></span> up early.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p>The second verb is in the <strong>-ing</strong> form in the past, too.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>When I was a child, I <span><strong>hated going</strong></span> to school. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>When I was a child, I <span><strong>hated went</strong></span> to school. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>-ing</strong> spelling</h4> <p>You can check the spelling of the <strong>-ing</strong> form of the verbs in the table below.</p> <p><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-18880\" src=\"/media/uploads/ing-spelling.png\" alt=\"Educational chart displaying spelling rules for adding '-ing' to verbs, with examples for each rule.\" width=\"500\" height=\"337\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h2>Verbs + <strong>to</strong>-infinitive</h2> <p>Many verbs in English are followed by&nbsp;<strong>to</strong>-infinitive. Some of these verbs are <strong>forget, hope, learn, need, offer, plan, remember, start, want </strong>and<strong> would like</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I <span><strong>forgot to turn off</strong></span> the light.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>hope to see</strong> </span>you soon.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I<span><strong>‘m learning to drive</strong></span>.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>We <span><strong>need to arrive</strong></span> early.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>She <span><strong>offered to help</strong></span> us.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>We <span><strong>are planning to go</strong></span> to France.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Remember to lock</strong></span> the door.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>want to go</strong></span> home.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>would like to buy</strong></span> a new computer.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p>The second verb takes the <strong>to</strong>-infinitive form in the past too.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I <span><strong>wanted to go</strong></span> home. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>wanted to went</strong></span> home. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h4>Would like</h4> <p>The verb&nbsp;<a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/would-like/\"><strong>would like</strong></a>&nbsp;(or <strong>‘d like</strong>) is different from&nbsp;<strong>like</strong>. We use&nbsp;<strong>would like + to&nbsp;</strong>+ infinitive, and we normally use&nbsp;<strong>like</strong> + <strong>-ing&nbsp;</strong>verb to talk about general preference. </p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I<span><strong>‘d like to study</strong></span> English.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>I <span><strong>like studying</strong></span> English.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p>The meaning is also different.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I<strong><span>‘d like to study</span></strong> English.&nbsp;</em>(=I want to do it.)</li> <li><em>I <span><strong>like studying</strong></span> English. </em>(=I enjoy it.)</li> </ul> <p>We use the question&nbsp;<strong>would you like…</strong> when we offer or suggest something.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em><span><strong>Would you like</strong></span> a cup of coffee?</em></li> <li><em><span><strong>Would you like</strong></span> to dance with me?</em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":550,"questions":[{"id":4742,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Pam loves <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> letters. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["receiving","receive","receivings"]}]},{"id":4743,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>She's planning <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> on a trip to Paris.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["going","to go","to going"]}]},{"id":4744,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Would you like <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> a picnic?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["have","having","to have"]}]},{"id":4745,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>My son never wants <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to bed. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["goes","going","to go"]}]},{"id":4746,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I don't mind <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the dishes.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["to wash","washing","wash"]}]},{"id":4747,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Sorry, I forgot <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you this afternoon. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["call","calling","to call"]}]},{"id":4748,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Do you like <span data-gap=\"0\"></span>?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["drive","driving","to driving"]}]},{"id":4749,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Please, remember <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> me the information that I need. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["to send","send","sending"]}]},{"id":4750,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I'd like <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you some questions. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["asking","ask","to ask"]}]},{"id":4751,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I learned <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the guitar when I was 6. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["played","playing","to play"]}]}]},{"id":551,"questions":[{"id":4752,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>When I was a child, I hated ______ to school.</div>","choices":[{"id":7246,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>went</span>"},{"id":7247,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>going</span>"},{"id":7248,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>go</span>"}]},{"id":4753,"num":"2","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I hope _____ a good lawyer. </div>","choices":[{"id":7249,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>find</span>"},{"id":7250,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>to find</span>"},{"id":7251,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>finding</span>"}]},{"id":4754,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He's very unfit; he needs _____ more exercise. </div>","choices":[{"id":7252,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>to do</span>"},{"id":7253,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>does</span>"},{"id":7254,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>doing</span>"}]},{"id":4755,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>A: 'Would you like _____?' B: 'No, thanks. I don't like _____.'</div>","choices":[{"id":7255,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>dancing / dancing</span>"},{"id":7256,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>dancing / to dance</span>"},{"id":7257,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>to dance / dancing</span>"}]},{"id":4756,"num":"5","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I don't like _____ early, but I need ______ it. </div>","choices":[{"id":7258,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>getting up / to do</span>"},{"id":7259,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>to get up / doing</span>"},{"id":7260,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>getting up / doing</span>"}]},{"id":4757,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I don't mind _____, but we need the car today because it's late. </div>","choices":[{"id":7261,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>walk</span>"},{"id":7262,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>to walk</span>"},{"id":7263,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>walking</span>"}]},{"id":4758,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>When did you learn _____?</div>","choices":[{"id":7264,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>swam</span>"},{"id":7265,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>to swim</span>"},{"id":7266,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>swimming</span>"}]},{"id":4759,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>My car was at the mechanic and she offered _____ me home. </div>","choices":[{"id":7267,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>to drive</span>"},{"id":7268,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>driving</span>"},{"id":7269,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>drove</span>"}]},{"id":4760,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>My dog loves _____ with other dogs. </div>","choices":[{"id":7270,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>play</span>"},{"id":7271,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>playing</span>"},{"id":7272,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>plays</span>"}]},{"id":4761,"num":"10","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>He plans _____ in Boston next year. </div>","choices":[{"id":7273,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>to stay</span>"},{"id":7274,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>staying</span>"},{"id":7275,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>stays</span>"}]}]},{"id":552,"questions":[{"id":4762,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Please, turn on the TV. I want <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the football match. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4763,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I don't mind <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> my English homework. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4764,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Did you remember <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the plants?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4765,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I don't like <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> in an office. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4766,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I hope <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> you soon. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4767,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The food is delicious. Where did you learn <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> this dish?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4768,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I need <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> very early tomorrow morning. I start work at 7 a.m.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4769,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I think I forgot <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the windows. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4770,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Do you like <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> football?</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":4771,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>We'd like <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> football this afternoon. </p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}